@page "/components/tree-grid"
@using Stil.Docs.Examples.TreeGrid

<DocsHeader Title="Tree grid" Eyebrow="Data">
    <Lead>Rows with rows below them, in columns: budgets, org charts, bills of materials and folders.</Lead>
</DocsHeader>

<p>
    <code>StilTreeGrid</code> is a <a href="components/data-grid">data grid</a> for items with children. It takes the same
    columns, with their sorting, filters, formats, editing and totals; sorting orders the rows under each parent. It
    follows the WAI-ARIA treegrid pattern: the grid is one tab stop, Up and Down move between rows, Right expands a row
    or moves to its first child, Left collapses it or moves to its parent, and Home and End jump to the first and last
    row. For a plain list of nested items, use the <a href="components/tree-view">tree view</a>.
</p>

<h2 id="totals">Totals that roll up</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(Budget)">
    <p>
        <code>Items</code> are the top-level rows and <code>ChildrenSelector</code> returns a row's children.
        A row with children shows, in each column with an <code>Aggregate</code>, the total of the rows below it that have
        no children of their own; the footer adds up all of those. <code>ExpandedLevels</code> chooses how many levels
        start expanded, and <code>ExpandAllAsync</code> and <code>CollapseAllAsync</code> open and close every row.
        A filter keeps the matching rows with all rows below them, and opens the rows above them.
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="load-on-demand">Children loaded on demand</h2>
<DocExample Type="typeof(LazyFolders)">
    <p>
        <code>LoadChildren</code> loads a row's children the first time it is expanded, while the row shows a spinner.
        <code>HasChildren</code> tells which rows get an expand toggle before their children are known; a row whose loaded
        children are none shows as a leaf. With both <code>ChildrenSelector</code> and <code>LoadChildren</code>, a
        selector that returns null means "not loaded yet".
    </p>
</DocExample>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<p>
    The tree grid also has the data grid's parameters, except grouping and <code>ItemsProvider</code>. It shows every
    row without a pager by default (<code>PageSize</code> 0).
</p>
<ApiTable Type="typeof(StilTreeGrid<>)" />
